{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>If you afflict, you shall afflict him.</b> It should say אוֹתָם (them), and what is the meaning of the doubling — עַנֵּה תְעַנֶּה (afflict, you shall afflict), צָעֹק יִצְעַק (cry out, he shall cry out), שָׁמֹעַ אֶשְׁמַע (hear, I shall hear)? And by way of the plain sense we may say: sometimes a person afflicts the orphan alone, while his mother the widow sees with her eyes and agonizes, yet has no power to save her son. And through the affliction of one of them, both of them are afflicted, and both of them cry out, and the Holy One, blessed be He, hears them both and punishes him doubly — so that his sons become orphans and his wife a widow. And by way of allusion we may say: since the Holy One, blessed be He, is the father of orphans, if so, surely in all their trouble He is troubled, as it were. Therefore He said אִם עַנֵּה — then תְעַנֶּה, you shall also afflict אוֹתוֹ, meaning Him who is the father of orphans. And behold, both of them cry out: the attribute of judgment indicts Him on high, and the orphan cries out below, and the Holy One, blessed be He, the Merciful One, receives the outcry of them both."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:22:21.386310852Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}